1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,220
Listen to a talk in a biology class.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:09,140
Man: The phenomenon of animal migration is a fascinating subject in biology.

3
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:14,472
Migration involves the regular, often seasonal movement of animals from one region to another,

4
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:18,280
typically in search of food, breeding grounds, or better climates.

5
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:22,080
This behavior is observed in a wide variety of species

6
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,160
including birds, mammals, fish, and insects.

7
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:29,230
One of the most well known examples is the migration of monarch butterflies.

8
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:36,120
These butterflies travel thousands of miles from North America to central Mexico to escape the cold winter.

9
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,560
This journey involves multiple generations

10
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,120
as no single butterfly makes the round trip.

11
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:45,060
Another remarkable example is the migration of humpback whales.

12
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:50,900
These massive creatures travel from their feeding grounds in polar waters to warmer tropical regions

13
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,180
where they breed and give birth.

14
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:56,235
Birds like the Arctic tern undertake one of the longest migrations,

15
00:00:56,235 --> 00:01:00,290
traveling from the Arctic to the Antarctic and back each year.

16
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:02,855
Despite their differences in size,

17
00:01:02,855 --> 00:01:09,010
species and reasons for migrating, they all migrate vast distances with precision.

18
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:13,330
They navigate like seasoned human pilots flying transcontinental routes,

19
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:16,210
only without aircraft, instruments or GPS.

20
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:19,250
Of course, migration is not without its challenges.

21
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:21,483
Animals must navigate vast distances,

22
00:01:21,483 --> 00:01:24,900
often facing predators, adverse weather

23
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,290
and human made obstacles like buildings and roads.

24
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:35,110
Protecting habitats and reducing human interference can help maintain the delicate balance that allows migration to occur.

25
00:01:35,110 --> 00:01:39,916
Understanding animal migration provides insight into the complex behaviors

26
00:01:39,916 --> 00:01:43,120
and survival strategies of various species.
